  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "**Example avatars with the issue:**\n\navtr_4eb89e8c-d454-4721-ad2b-6450d681c979\n\navtr_ec8ebab2-337e-4c87-a91e-9147772f6fdc\n\n**Description:**\n\nThere is a behavior setup on those avatars changing the tracking state depending on the upright value. This is causing a bug where the physbones on the left foot are not being affected by gravity nor colliding with the floor.\n\n**Repro steps:**\n\n- Load into the specific avatar with locomotion animations enabled.\n\n- Stand up above .9 upright and look at left foot, it should be behaving normally.\n\n- Crouch down below .9 upright and look at left foot, now it is not being affected by gravity nor the floor plane collider.\n\nDisabling locomotion animations fixes the issue.\n\n**Video with the Issue:**\n\nhttps://files.catbox.moe/1crfev.mp4",
